        "id": 18294,
        "name": "DoobleGem",
        "username": "DoobleGem",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/a4c791/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-07-28T12:04:09.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>A-hey there! Firstly, just want to say I'm super-duper excited to play Oblivaeon! Done a few practise runs with some of the new Heroes and Environments first, but today my friends and myself are planning on taking on the big man himself!</p><p>Hooowever there is one thing I'm wanting to check first, to make sure I'm getting things right. At their core, the Battle Zones seem quite simple - characters and cards from one Battle Zone can't interact with characters and cards from another, unless explicitally stated. Got it!</p><p>Wwwhat I'm less ure about is how cards which attach to other targets or play areas work. A few examples come to mind, such as Captain Cosmic. If he gives a character in his zone Cosmic Weapon, if he leaves to go to another Battle Zone, does his Cosmic Weapon still work? Or because it's in his ally's play area, does Cosmic Weapon count as being in one Battle Zone and still work, whilst Captain Cosmic himself is in another?</p><p>Then you have cases of cards you play on non-allies. For example, if Mainstay got a Scion in a Headlock, then left the Battle Zone, is he still Headlocking that Scion but like... with the world's stretchiest arms? Or does that card essentially become blank, until Mainstay returns to the Battle Zone, at which point he springs straight back into Headlocking that card?</p><p>Any help on the matter would be much appreciated!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:51:35.538Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
