        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>A-hey there! Firstly, just want to say I&#39;m super-duper excited to play Oblivaeon! Done a few practise runs with some of the new Heroes and Environments first, but today my friends and myself are planning on taking on the big man himself!</p><p>Hooowever there is one thing I&#39;m wanting to check first, to make sure I&#39;m getting things right. At their core, the Battle Zones seem quite simple - characters and cards from one Battle Zone can&#39;t interact with characters and cards from another, unless explicitally stated. Got it!</p><p>Wwwhat I&#39;m less ure about is how cards which attach to other targets or play areas work. A few examples come to mind, such as Captain Cosmic. If he gives a character in his zone Cosmic Weapon, if he leaves to go to another Battle Zone, does his Cosmic Weapon still work? Or because it&#39;s in his ally&#39;s play area, does Cosmic Weapon count as being in one Battle Zone and still work, whilst Captain Cosmic himself is in another?</p><p>Then you have cases of cards you play on non-allies. For example, if Mainstay got a Scion in a Headlock, then left the Battle Zone, is he still Headlocking that Scion but like... with the world&#39;s stretchiest arms? Or does that card essentially become blank, until Mainstay returns to the Battle Zone, at which point he springs straight back into Headlocking that card?</p><p>Any help on the matter would be much appreciated!</p>",
