        "raw": "<p>It depends on the wording of the individual cards.</p><p>The Cosmic Weapon will work for the hero who has it because it&#39;s the weapon itself that gives the power. Destructive Response however would not &quot;see&quot; the Construct&#39;s destruction if Cap was in the other battle zone (even though it would end up in Cap&#39;s trash when destroyed).</p><p>Similarly Chrono-Ranger&#39;s By Any Means would increase damage dealt to the target no matter where Chrono-Ranger was, but The Ultimate Target would try to trigger the extra power but if Jim isn&#39;t in the the same battlezone then it wont &quot;find&quot; him.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I don&#39;t have my copies yet but doesn&#39;t Headlock have a clause on it about not being able to redirect damage destroying it?</p>",
